      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "pageStart": 10,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-000-1-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "A typical enterprise’s infrastructure has grown increasingly complex. A single enterprise may \noperate several internal networks, remote offices with their own local infrastructure, remote \nand/or mobile individuals, and cloud services. This complexity has outstripped legacy methods \nof perimeter-based network security as there is no single, easily identified perimeter for the \nenterprise. Perimeter-based network security has also been shown to be insufficient since once \nattackers breach the perimeter, further lateral movement is unhindered. \nThis complex enterprise has led to the development",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
